# grafana/dashboard-linter exclusions.
#
# The two rule lists below are intentionally identical: dashboard-linter
# requires per-rule exclusion entries (no per-panel disable-multiple), so
# every redis_exporter panel is listed once per disabled rule.
#
# Drift between this file and transport.json panel titles is detected by
# TestDashboardLintExclusionsMatchRealPanels in dashboard_lint_test.go —
# stale entries fail Tier 1 CI rather than silently no-op.
exclusions:
  target-job-rule:
    reason: |
      These panels query the redis_exporter sidecar's own Prometheus
      scrape job (job="redis"), not the mercure hub `$job`. Adding
      `$job` would change semantics and break the multi-stack
      compose setup.
      Re-evaluate if/when redis_exporter is scraped by the same
      Prometheus job as the hub (then `$job` applies and the
      exclusion can be removed).
    entries:
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Memory used vs max
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Evictions / rejected connections
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Commands per second
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Connected clients
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Keyspace hit ratio
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Slow log length
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Network throughput
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: CPU usage
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Top 5 commands by avg latency
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Memory fragmentation
  target-instance-rule:
    reason: |
      redis_exporter scrapes exactly one target per backend; an
      `$instance` filter would never narrow the query in a useful
      way.
      Re-evaluate if/when the hub-to-exporter mapping becomes
      many-to-one or many-to-many (then `$instance` becomes
      meaningful and the exclusion can be removed).
    entries:
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Memory used vs max
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Evictions / rejected connections
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Commands per second
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Connected clients
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Keyspace hit ratio
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Slow log length
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Network throughput
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: CPU usage
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Top 5 commands by avg latency
      - dashboard: Mercure Redis Transport
        panel: Memory fragmentation
